                <pb facs="0347" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.5151/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-01T13:00:00+02:00">October 1, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 2—4:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1500. My 1496, September 30, 6 p.m. The Legation has received a note from the
                    Foreign Office confirming the telephone message mentioned in the Legation’s
                    telegram under reference to the effect that pending a final decision on the
                    matter American nationals and firms in Egypt will be exempt from declaring their
                    dollar holdings in Egypt and abroad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
